    "https://nwmissouri.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Northwest-Missouri-State-University-Maryville/Assistant-Professor-of-History_R-00057": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of History",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSALARY: $56,827.00 POSITION TITLE: Assistant Professor of History DEPARTMENT : History JOB DESCRIPTION: PRIMARY DUTY: The School of Humanities and Social Sciences at Northwest Missouri State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of History with a specialization in Public History and a demonstrated emphasis in museum studies, to begin January 6, 2027. We seek a dynamic teacher-scholar committed to undergraduate education, profession-based learning, and community engagement. The successful candidate will lead the university’s undergraduate minor in Public History and Museum Studies and will contribute to the department’s broader curriculum in history. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Teach a 4:4 course load, including introductory and upper-level courses, including graduate level courses, in U.S. history, public history, and the candidate’s area of historical specialization. Direct the undergraduate minor in Public History and Museum Studies. Supervise and mentor students in hands-on, project-based learning environments. Manage and oversee the university’s Public History Lab, including training students in the use of specialized equipment such as dry mount presses. Coordinate exhibitions in designated gallery spaces within the Humanities & Social Sciences building. Collaborate closely with the university archives and campus museums to support student learning opportunities and community access to these spaces. Build and sustain partnerships with regional cultural institutions, including museums, historical societies, and other heritage and tourism organizations. Maintain an active program of scholarship in public history and/or the candidate’s field of specialization. Participate in departmental, college, and university service. Perform other duties as assigned REQUIREMENTS: Education: Ph.D. in History or related field (ABD considered with completion by May 2027). Certification/License: N/A              Experience: Prior experience in classroom and online instruction in History Skills: Demonstrated experience or training in public history, with a focus on museum practice; evidence of effective undergraduate teaching or strong potential for excellence in the classroom; commitment to student mentorship and profession-based learning. WORKING CONDITIONS: The position entails classroom and/or online instruction in General Education and upper division courses typically ranging from 15 to 60 students.  Faculty maintain regular office hours within the department area to support students.           SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: Program coordinator for a growing Public History and Museum Studies program EQUIPMENT/MATERIALS USED: All classrooms are technology-enhanced (document stations, video equipment, wireless Internet access). Online courses are offered using Canvas, Northwest’s Learning Management System.   TYPICAL PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Ability to meet essential pedagogical and classroom functions APPLICATION MATERIALS: A complete application consists of: 1) a letter describing your teaching experience and suitability for the position; 2) a current curriculum vitae; 3) transcripts; and 4) contact information, including telephone numbers and e-mail addresses, for three references.  Applications will be reviewed beginning October 1, 2026. INQUIRIES FOR THE POSITION CAN BE MADE TO:          Dr. Dawn Gilley, Discipline Lead       School of Humanities and Social Sciences       Northwest Missouri State University       800 University Drive       Maryville, MO 64468       (660) 562-1839        dgilley@nwmissouri.edu or       Dr. Jessica Gracey, School Chair       School of Humanities and Social Sciences       Northwest Missouri State University       800 University Drive       Maryville, MO 64468       (660) 562-1290        jessicag@nwmissouri.edu COMMUNITY: Northwest Missouri State University located in Maryville, Missouri, a community of 12,000 with a diverse economy and a strong industrial base. Maryville is located 45 miles north of St. Joseph, Missouri, 90 miles north of Kansas City, Missouri, and 110 miles southeast of Omaha, Nebraska. For more information visit the city’s website at www.maryville.org . UNIVERSITY: With an enrollment of more than 8,500 students, Northwest is a coeducational, primarily residential four-year university that offers a broad range of undergraduate and selected graduate programs on its Maryville campus and through Northwest Online .   Founded in 1905, Northwest boasts a high retention rate and a graduation rate in the 95th percentile among its peers. Additionally, results of the Ruffalo Noel Levitz Student Satisfaction Inventory show Northwest students are more satisfied than students at national peers, and 78 percent of Northwest students report they would repeat their university experience, compared to 75 percent of students surveyed nationally at their respective institutions.   Furthermore, the University is a national model for student success and career placement with 93 percent of bachelor’s degree earners and 98 percent of master’s degree earners securing employment or continuing their education within six months of completing a degree at Northwest, according to the most recent data .    Northwest places a high emphasis on profession-based learning to help graduates get a jumpstart on their careers while maintaining competitive tuition rates and generous financial assistance to help minimize the financial barriers students may face when pursuing a college degree.   Students have opportunities to build their résumés with experiences on campus in nearly every area of study, including the  Horace Mann Laboratory School ,  National Public Radio affiliate KXCV , the R.T. Wright Farm ,  Mozingo Outdoor Education Recreation Area ,  a partnership with the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency or  Knacktive , a student-driven integrated digital marketing communications agency. In conjunction with its emergency and disaster management program, Northwest organizes and hosts Missouri Hope , an annual mass casualty training exercise that attracts first responders and emergency workers from throughout the nation and provides hands-on training in preparation for a natural disaster.   The University’s vibrant and diverse learning community also offers more than 150 student organizations, and  textbooks and a laptop are included  in tuition, saving students an estimated $6,900 over four years. Northwest offers 1,200 student employment positions, allowing students to build professional skills through its internationally benchmarked student employment program.    For more information about Northwest and its performance, visit  www.nwmissouri.edu/aboutus/facts/ ."
    },
    "https://nwmissouri.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Northwest-Missouri-State-University-Maryville/Director-of-Payroll-Services_R-00230": {
      "title": "Director of Payroll Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSALARY: $75,270.00 POSITION TITLE: Director of Payroll Services DEPARTMENT : University Finance JOB DESCRIPTION: EMPLOYMENT TERMS: Full-time position PRIMARY DUTY:   The Payroll Director is responsible for the strategic leadership, administration, and oversight of the University’s payroll operations, ensuring accurate and timely bi-weekly payroll processing for faculty, staff, student employees, and temporary personnel. This position ensures compliance with all federal, state, and local payroll regulations and serves as the functional lead for payroll operations within the University’s newly implemented Workday Human Capital Management (HCM) and Payroll system. The Payroll Director collaborates closely with Human Resources, Finance, Information Technology, and external auditors to maintain operational excellence, system integrity, compliance, and continuous process improvement. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Payroll Administration & Operations Actively perform and coordinate all payroll operations for the University, including bi-weekly payroll processing for all employee groups. Ensure timely and accurate processing of earnings, deductions, taxes, garnishments, benefits, and leave accruals. Lead payroll reconciliation processes, payroll accounting entries, and year-end reporting activities including W-2 preparation. Develop, implement, enhance and maintain payroll policies, procedures, and internal controls to ensure operational efficiency and compliance. Monitor payroll workflows and deadlines to ensure uninterrupted payroll services. Compliance & Regulatory Oversight Ensure compliance with all applicable federal, state, and local laws related to payroll administration, including: Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) IRS regulations State wage and hour laws Retirement and benefits reporting requirements Manage payroll tax filings and coordinate audits with internal and external auditors. Maintain confidentiality and security of employee payroll records and sensitive information. Stay current on legislative and regulatory changes impacting payroll operations and recommend necessary policy or system updates. Workday Payroll System Leadership Serve as the functional owner and subject matter expert for Workday Payroll and related Human Capital Management (HCM) modules. Lead ongoing optimization, configuration review, testing, upgrades, and troubleshooting within the newly implemented Workday environment. Partner with Human Resources, Information Technology, and Finance teams to improve system functionality and automate payroll processes. Develop and maintain payroll reporting and analytics using Workday reporting and other tools, including Microsoft Excel. Coordinate and complete system testing for patches, upgrades, and regulatory updates. Leadership & Team Management Supervise and mentor payroll staff, fostering a culture of accountability, customer service, and continuous improvement. Establish performance expectations and provide ongoing coaching and professional development opportunities. Collaborate with campus departments to resolve payroll-related issues and provide training on payroll processes and Workday functionality. Strategic Planning & Process Improvement Evaluate payroll operations and recommend enhancements to improve accuracy, efficiency, and employee experience. Participate in strategic initiatives related to Finance, Human Resources, and enterprise systems. Develop metrics and reporting tools to monitor payroll performance and compliance risks. REQUIRMENTS: Education:   Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or related field. Experience: Minimum of 3–5 years of progressively responsible payroll experience, preferably in higher education or a complex multi-department organization. Minimum of 1–3 years of supervisory or leadership experience. Strong knowledge of payroll laws, tax regulations, wage and hour compliance, and payroll accounting. Experience processing payrolls with multiple employee classifications. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to collaborate across departments. Demonstrated ability to manage confidential information with discretion and professionalism. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Advanced understanding of payroll systems, payroll accounting, and Human Resources Information Systems (HRIS) platforms. Strong proficiency with Microsoft Excel and financial reporting tools. Ability to interpret complex regulations and apply them operationally. Strong project management and organizational leadership capabilities. Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment. WORKING CONDITIONS: Standard office environment with extended periods of computer work. Occasional evening or weekend work may be required during payroll processing cycles, fiscal year-end, or system upgrades. EQUIPMENT/MATERIALS USED: Personal computer with appropriate software applications and with internet, networking and mainframe capabilities, copier, telephone with conferencing capabilities, and other office equipment. TYPICAL PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Requires manual dexterity sufficient to operate standard office machines; light lifting; normal range of hearing and vision. COMMUNITY: Northwest Missouri State University located in Maryville, Missouri, a community of 12,000 with a diverse economy and a strong industrial base. Maryville is located 45 miles north of St. Joseph, Missouri, 90 miles north of Kansas City, Missouri, and 110 miles southeast of Omaha, Nebraska. For more information visit the city’s website at www.maryville.org . UNIVERSITY: With an enrollment of more than 8,500 students, Northwest is a coeducational, primarily residential four-year university that offers a broad range of undergraduate and selected graduate programs on its Maryville campus and through Northwest Online .   Founded in 1905, Northwest boasts a high retention rate and a graduation rate in the 95th percentile among its peers. Additionally, results of the Ruffalo Noel Levitz Student Satisfaction Inventory show Northwest students are more satisfied than students at national peers, and 78 percent of Northwest students report they would repeat their university experience, compared to 75 percent of students surveyed nationally at their respective institutions.   Furthermore, the University is a national model for student success and career placement with 93 percent of bachelor’s degree earners and 98 percent of master’s degree earners securing employment or continuing their education within six months of completing a degree at Northwest, according to the most recent data .    Northwest places a high emphasis on profession-based learning to help graduates get a jumpstart on their careers while maintaining competitive tuition rates and generous financial assistance to help minimize the financial barriers students may face when pursuing a college degree.   Students have opportunities to build their résumés with experiences on campus in nearly every area of study, including the  Horace Mann Laboratory School ,  National Public Radio affiliate KXCV , the R.T. Wright Farm ,  Mozingo Outdoor Education Recreation Area ,  a partnership with the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency or  Knacktive , a student-driven integrated digital marketing communications agency. In conjunction with its emergency and disaster management program, Northwest organizes and hosts Missouri Hope , an annual mass casualty training exercise that attracts first responders and emergency workers from throughout the nation and provides hands-on training in preparation for a natural disaster.   The University’s vibrant and diverse learning community also offers more than 150 student organizations, and  textbooks and a laptop are included  in tuition, saving students an estimated $6,900 over four years. Northwest offers 1,200 student employment positions, allowing students to build professional skills through its internationally benchmarked student employment program.    For more information about Northwest and its performance, visit  www.nwmissouri.edu/aboutus/facts/ ."
    },
    "https://nwmissouri.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Northwest-Missouri-State-University-Maryville/Donor-Experience-Officer_R-00225": {
      "title": "Donor Experience Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSALARY: $47,633.00 POSITION TITLE: Donor Experience Officer DEPARTMENT : University Advancement JOB DESCRIPTION: EMPLOYMENT TERMS: Full time, 12 month         PRIMARY DUTY: The Donor Experience Officer (DXO) builds and matures the leadership annual giving pipeline by managing a high-volume portfolio of prospects through the entire donor journey. Utilizing modern digital communication tools including personalized video, text, phone, and email campaigns. The DXO delivers targeted, authentic outreach to increase donor retention, acquisition, and pipeline growth. The DXO collaborates with advancement staff, university marketing, and campus leadership to align outreach strategies with institutional priorities. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Portfolio Management: Actively qualifies, cultivates, and stewardship-manages a digital portfolio of 800+ prospects and leadership annual donors. Omnichannel Digital Outreach: Leverages text, personalized video platforms, email, phone, and social media to execute high-volume, meaningful touches that build donor affinity. Pipeline Development: Serves as a primary prospect identifier; strategically moves annual donors through the donation pipeline and transitions qualified major gift prospects to development staff members. Annual Giving Partnership: Partners with the AVP to execute targeted segments of the annual appeal program, focusing on donor acquisition and upgrading average gift amounts. Data & CRM Excellence: Systematically tracks all donor interactions in the CRM; utilizes data and engagement analytics to refine outreach strategies and measure campaign effectiveness. Student Talent Management: Recruits, trains, and supervises DXO student interns, fostering a collaborative, metrics-driven student outreach environment. Donor Stewardship: In coordination with advancement staff, delivers exceptional, proactive customer service to alumni, donors, and stakeholders related to event outreach. Institutional Engagement: Performs other duties as assigned, including assisting with and attending key university advancement events.   REQUIREMENTS: Education: Bachelor’s degree required. Experience: One (1) year of experience in fundraising, digital sales, public relations, alumni relations, or a related relationship-management field. Skills & Abilities: Superior interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, with comfort being \"on camera\" for personalized video outreach. Strong technological aptitude, including experience with CRM databases and digital communication platforms. Exceptional organizational and multi-project management skills; ability to work independently in a fast-paced, metrics-driven environment. High emotional intelligence and the ability to engage authentically with high-profile constituents, alumni, and campus partners. WORKING CONDITIONS:                  This position requires participation in events on occasion outside of normal working hours    SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: Requires leadership responsibilities, including supervising students EQUIPMENT/MATERIALS USED:                   Knowledge and experience with database management software and audio/visual and computer technologies required TYPICAL PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Able to carry and set-up audio/visual equipment and lift up to 20 pounds . COMMUNITY: Northwest Missouri State University located in Maryville, Missouri, a community of 12,000 with a diverse economy and a strong industrial base. Maryville is located 45 miles north of St. Joseph, Missouri, 90 miles north of Kansas City, Missouri, and 110 miles southeast of Omaha, Nebraska. For more information visit the city’s website at www.maryville.org . UNIVERSITY: With an enrollment of more than 8,500 students, Northwest is a coeducational, primarily residential four-year university that offers a broad range of undergraduate and selected graduate programs on its Maryville campus and through Northwest Online .   Founded in 1905, Northwest boasts a high retention rate and a graduation rate in the 95th percentile among its peers. Additionally, results of the Ruffalo Noel Levitz Student Satisfaction Inventory show Northwest students are more satisfied than students at national peers, and 78 percent of Northwest students report they would repeat their university experience, compared to 75 percent of students surveyed nationally at their respective institutions.   Furthermore, the University is a national model for student success and career placement with 93 percent of bachelor’s degree earners and 98 percent of master’s degree earners securing employment or continuing their education within six months of completing a degree at Northwest, according to the most recent data .    Northwest places a high emphasis on profession-based learning to help graduates get a jumpstart on their careers while maintaining competitive tuition rates and generous financial assistance to help minimize the financial barriers students may face when pursuing a college degree.   Students have opportunities to build their résumés with experiences on campus in nearly every area of study, including the  Horace Mann Laboratory School ,  National Public Radio affiliate KXCV , the R.T. Wright Farm ,  Mozingo Outdoor Education Recreation Area ,  a partnership with the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency or  Knacktive , a student-driven integrated digital marketing communications agency. In conjunction with its emergency and disaster management program, Northwest organizes and hosts Missouri Hope , an annual mass casualty training exercise that attracts first responders and emergency workers from throughout the nation and provides hands-on training in preparation for a natural disaster.   The University’s vibrant and diverse learning community also offers more than 150 student organizations, and  textbooks and a laptop are included  in tuition, saving students an estimated $6,900 over four years. Northwest offers 1,200 student employment positions, allowing students to build professional skills through its internationally benchmarked student employment program.    For more information about Northwest and its performance, visit  www.nwmissouri.edu/aboutus/facts/ ."
    },
    "https://nwmissouri.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Northwest-Missouri-State-University-Maryville/Associate-Teacher--Infant-Toddler-Center_R-00229": {
      "title": "Associate Teacher, Infant Toddler Center",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSALARY: $35,941.00 POSITION TITLE: ITC: Associate Teacher DEPARTMENT : Leet Infant and Toddler Center JOB DESCRIPTION: EMPLOYMENT TERMS: Full-time position PRIMARY DUTY: The ITC Associate Teacher will serve as a teacher and educational leader in an early childhood laboratory school environment which values child-centered care and education practices. The ITC Associate Teacher should possess high energy and the ability to handle the demands of infants and toddlers with different personalities and needs. This position will design and implement curriculum to meet the social, emotional, physical, communication and cognitive needs of children based on the National Association for the Education of Young Children accreditation standards and a Reggio-inspired philosophy of learning. This position is responsible for promoting high standards for care and teaching of young children, communicating effectively with parents, curriculum design, and collaboration with the Leet Center, Horace Mann, and School of Education faculty and staff. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: 1. Collaborate with ITC colleagues for the best interest of the infants and toddlers within the ITC classroom 2. Be responsible for the overall daily operation of the infant/toddler classroom 3. Be responsible for the health, safety, and well-being of infants and toddlers 4. Be responsible for creating an environment that is nurturing, developmentally appropriate, and allows for exploration and investigation 5. Collaborate with the School of Education Early Childhood faculty for the placement and mentorship of University Early Childhood students 6. Mentor and coach the Early Childhood students by offering positive guidance, constructive feedback, and support throughout their practicum experiences 7. Mentor and coach student employees by offering positive guidance, constructive feedback, and support 8. Build and maintain working relationships with parents, families, caregivers and other Horace Mann and Leet Center colleagues 9. Participate in professional development opportunities when needed and/or as they arise 10. Participate in after school committees, parent meetings, and faculty meetings, as assigned 11. Participate in University, School, department and discipline accreditation processes (DESE, AAQEP, HLC, NAEYC) and related duties to ensure continuous quality improvement 12. Support the Director of Horace Mann & Leet Center and Assistant Director of the Leet Center in earning and maintaining state licensure and operational safety training and protocols 13. Perform other duties as assigned REQUIREMENTS: Education: Bachelor’s degree in Education, Early Childhood Education, or other closely related associated program OR Five or more years of experience in childcare Experience: Experience in childcare; knowledge of Constructivist Philosophy, Reggio Emilia Approach, and Conscious Discipline; experience in a collaborative setting Skills: Ability to collaborate with others; communication skills; general technology skills; ability to mentor and coach University students WORKING CONDITIONS: Collaborative team-based academic environment in a university-based laboratory school SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: Will assist with the supervision of observation students, practicum students, and student employees EQUIPMENT/MATERIALS USED: laptop, iPad TYPICAL PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Actively instructing and monitoring infants and toddlers in the classroom and in the outdoor classroom. Ability to push and pull wheeled equipment. Must be able sit, stand, squat, twist, turn, to meet the care demands of working with young children. Must be able to lift up to 30 pounds, sitting and standing for extended periods of time, and navigate steps and ramps with young children. COMMUNITY: Northwest Missouri State University located in Maryville, Missouri, a community of 12,000 with a diverse economy and a strong industrial base. Maryville is located 45 miles north of St. Joseph, Missouri, 90 miles north of Kansas City, Missouri, and 110 miles southeast of Omaha, Nebraska. For more information visit the city’s website at www.maryville.org . UNIVERSITY: With an enrollment of more than 8,500 students, Northwest is a coeducational, primarily residential four-year university that offers a broad range of undergraduate and selected graduate programs on its Maryville campus and through Northwest Online .   Founded in 1905, Northwest boasts a high retention rate and a graduation rate in the 95th percentile among its peers. Additionally, results of the Ruffalo Noel Levitz Student Satisfaction Inventory show Northwest students are more satisfied than students at national peers, and 78 percent of Northwest students report they would repeat their university experience, compared to 75 percent of students surveyed nationally at their respective institutions.   Furthermore, the University is a national model for student success and career placement with 93 percent of bachelor’s degree earners and 98 percent of master’s degree earners securing employment or continuing their education within six months of completing a degree at Northwest, according to the most recent data .    Northwest places a high emphasis on profession-based learning to help graduates get a jumpstart on their careers while maintaining competitive tuition rates and generous financial assistance to help minimize the financial barriers students may face when pursuing a college degree.   Students have opportunities to build their résumés with experiences on campus in nearly every area of study, including the  Horace Mann Laboratory School ,  National Public Radio affiliate KXCV , the R.T. Wright Farm ,  Mozingo Outdoor Education Recreation Area ,  a partnership with the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency or  Knacktive , a student-driven integrated digital marketing communications agency. In conjunction with its emergency and disaster management program, Northwest organizes and hosts Missouri Hope , an annual mass casualty training exercise that attracts first responders and emergency workers from throughout the nation and provides hands-on training in preparation for a natural disaster.   The University’s vibrant and diverse learning community also offers more than 150 student organizations, and  textbooks and a laptop are included  in tuition, saving students an estimated $6,900 over four years. Northwest offers 1,200 student employment positions, allowing students to build professional skills through its internationally benchmarked student employment program.    For more information about Northwest and its performance, visit  www.nwmissouri.edu/aboutus/facts/ ."
