      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Adjunct, Mass Media, School of Communication and Mass Media Department: Mass Media JM Job Description: EMPLOYMENT TERMS: Temporary, Adjunct PRIMARY DUTY: The School of Communication and Mass Media at Northwest Missouri State University is seeking candidates to create a pool of applicants who can teach as an Adjunct within the following Mass Media disciplines: Social Media Management, Mass Media, Broadcasting and Production, Multimedia Journalism, Sports Media, Advertising and Digital Media/Content Strategy. Classes may be in the Fall, Spring or Summer term. Classes may be held on-campus or online. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Teach courses within specific disciplines with the School of Communication & Mass Media Perform other duties as assigned REQUIREMENTS: Education: Graduate degree in specific discipline listed above with 18 hours in content area and/or credentials, qualifications and/or tested experience sufficient for HLC accreditation Certification/License: Driver’s license       Experience: Evidence of successful teaching in the discipline Skills: Skills and experience with instructional technology              WORKING CONDITIONS: This position will work in an academic environment with collaborative team-based faculty and have access to the Internet for online course sites and materials along with Northwest email.                      SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: NONE EQUIPMENT/MATERIALS USED: Laptops and other technology as necessary to provide outstanding instruction    TYPICAL PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Ability to complete essential classroom functions and the ability to lift up to 20 pounds. COMMUNITY: Northwest Missouri State University located in Maryville, Missouri, a community of 12,000 with a diverse economy and a strong industrial base. Maryville is located 45 miles north of St. Joseph, Missouri, 90 miles north of Kansas City, Missouri, and 110 miles southeast of